/**
 * Groups the contacts of a set of accounts by the domain of their email address.
 * The class runs with sharing, and the query uses USER_MODE, so the running
 * user's record sharing, object permissions and field-level security all apply.
 */
public with sharing class ContactDomainService {

    /**
     * Returns contacts of the given accounts grouped by lower-cased email domain.
     * Contacts with no email are left out.
     * Example: for Jane@Example.COM the key is example.com.
     *
     * @param accountIds Ids of the accounts whose contacts to group
     * @return map of domain to contacts; an empty map if the input is null or empty
     */
    public static Map<String, List<Contact>> groupByEmailDomain(Set<Id> accountIds) {
        Map<String, List<Contact>> result = new Map<String, List<Contact>>();

        if (accountIds == null || accountIds.isEmpty()) {
            return result;
        }

        // Drop a null entry so it is not passed into the bind variable.
        Set<Id> ids = new Set<Id>(accountIds);
        ids.remove(null);
        if (ids.isEmpty()) {
            return result;
        }

        // A plain for loop over the query result loads all rows at once.
        // Very large inputs could hit the heap limit, but the method has to
        // return every contact in the map anyway.
        for (Contact c : [
            SELECT Id, Email, AccountId
            FROM Contact
            WHERE AccountId IN :ids AND Email != null
            WITH USER_MODE
        ]) {
            String domain = extractDomain(c.Email);
            if (String.isBlank(domain)) {
                continue;
            }
            List<Contact> bucket = result.get(domain);
            if (bucket == null) {
                bucket = new List<Contact>();
                result.put(domain, bucket);
            }
            bucket.add(c);
        }

        return result;
    }

    /**
     * Returns the lower-cased text after the last '@', or null if there is
     * no usable domain.
     */
    private static String extractDomain(String email) {
        if (String.isBlank(email)) {
            return null;
        }
        String trimmed = email.trim();
        Integer at = trimmed.lastIndexOf('@');
        if (at < 0 || at == trimmed.length() - 1) {
            return null;
        }
        return trimmed.substring(at + 1).toLowerCase();
    }
}
```

**Notes**
- The class is declared `with sharing`, and the query uses `WITH USER_MODE`. Together they apply the running user's record sharing, object permissions and field-level security.
- If the user cannot read `Email` or `AccountId`, `USER_MODE` throws an exception. It does not return incomplete data.
- Contacts without an email are filtered out in the query (`Email != null`).
- The method runs a single query whatever the size of the input, so it is safe to call with many accounts.

The three exception classes share one base, so a caller can handle every terms error with a single `catch (PaymentTermsException e)`. `PaymentTerms` trims the input and then matches it case-insensitively.

