/**
 * Utility for reading the active values of a picklist or multi-select picklist
 * field. The object and field are chosen at runtime.
 */
public with sharing class PicklistService {

    public class PicklistServiceException extends Exception {}

    public class Option {
        @AuraEnabled public String value;
        @AuraEnabled public String label;
        @AuraEnabled public Boolean isDefault;

        public Option(String value, String label, Boolean isDefault) {
            this.value = value;
            this.label = label;
            this.isDefault = isDefault == true;
        }
    }

    /**
     * Returns the active values of the given picklist or multi-select picklist field,
     * in the order they are defined on the field.
     */
    public static List<Option> activeOptions(String objectApiName, String fieldApiName) {
        if (String.isBlank(objectApiName)) {
            throw new PicklistServiceException('Object API name is required.');
        }
        if (String.isBlank(fieldApiName)) {
            throw new PicklistServiceException('Field API name is required.');
        }

        String objName = objectApiName.trim();
        String fldName = fieldApiName.trim();

        Schema.SObjectField field;
        try {
            Schema.SObjectType sType = Schema.getGlobalDescribe().get(objName.toLowerCase());
            if (sType == null) {
                throw new PicklistServiceException('Object not found: ' + objName);
            }
            field = sType.getDescribe().fields.getMap().get(fldName.toLowerCase());
            if (field == null) {
                throw new PicklistServiceException(
                    'Field ' + fldName + ' not found on object ' + objName);
            }
        } catch (PicklistServiceException e) {
            throw e;
        } catch (Exception e) {
            throw new PicklistServiceException(
                'Unable to describe ' + objName + '.' + fldName + ': ' + e.getMessage());
        }

        Schema.DescribeFieldResult dfr = field.getDescribe();
        Schema.DisplayType fieldType = dfr.getType();
        if (fieldType != Schema.DisplayType.PICKLIST
                && fieldType != Schema.DisplayType.MULTIPICKLIST) {
            throw new PicklistServiceException(
                'Field ' + objName + '.' + fldName + ' is not a picklist or multi-select picklist.');
        }

        List<Option> result = new List<Option>();
        for (Schema.PicklistEntry entry : dfr.getPicklistValues()) {
            if (entry.isActive()) {
                result.add(new Option(entry.getValue(), entry.getLabel(), entry.isDefaultValue()));
            }
        }
        return result;
    }
}
```

**Notes:**
- Names are trimmed and lower-cased before lookup. The global describe and field maps are case-insensitive, so `account` / `INDUSTRY` resolve correctly.
- `getPicklistValues()` returns entries in the order they are defined on the field. Inactive entries are skipped using `isActive()`.
- Every failure is surfaced as `PicklistServiceException`: blank input, unknown object, unknown field, non-picklist type, and any unexpected describe error, which is wrapped.
- The method reads metadata only and no record data, so no CRUD/FLS check on records is needed.

Design notes:
- **Order number matching.** `Order_Number__c` on the order is always upper case, so the handler trims and upper-cases event values before querying and matching.
- **Sharing.** The platform event trigger runs as the Automated Process user. I use `without sharing` so integration updates are not blocked by record visibility. Field access is not enforced, which is acceptable for system automation.
- **Partial failures.** The handler uses `Database.update` with `allOrNone = false`. One bad record then doesn't fail the whole batch, and the failures are logged.
- **Retries.** The update repeats the same shipment data, so if the trigger is retried, applying an event twice gives the same result.

