The service validates the reason first, then loads the cases through the selector. It escalates every case that is not `Closed` and not already escalated. All writes go through one unit of work, which is committed only when at least one case changed.

File: force-app/main/default/classes/CaseEscalationService.cls
```apex
public with sharing class CaseEscalationService {

    public class EscalationException extends Exception {}

    private static final String STATUS_CLOSED = 'Closed';
    private static final String PRIORITY_HIGH = 'High';

    public static void escalate(Set<Id> caseIds, String reason) {
        if (String.isBlank(reason)) {
            throw new EscalationException('An escalation reason is required.');
        }
        if (caseIds == null || caseIds.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        List<Case> cases = CasesSelector.newInstance().selectById(caseIds);
        if (cases == null || cases.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        fflib_ISObjectUnitOfWork uow = null;
        Date dueDate = Date.today().addDays(1);

        for (Case c : cases) {
            if (c.Status == STATUS_CLOSED || c.IsEscalated == true) {
                continue;
            }
            if (uow == null) {
                uow = Application.UnitOfWork.newInstance();
            }

            c.IsEscalated = true;
            c.Priority = PRIORITY_HIGH;
            uow.registerDirty(c);

            Task t = new Task(
                Subject = 'Escalated: ' + reason,
                WhatId = c.Id,
                OwnerId = c.OwnerId,
                ActivityDate = dueDate,
                Priority = PRIORITY_HIGH
            );
            uow.registerNew(t);
        }

        if (uow != null) {
            uow.commitWork();
        }
    }
}
```

**Design notes:**
- **Lazy unit of work:** the unit of work is created only when the first case needs escalating. If none do, no unit of work exists and `commitWork()` is never called.
- **Selector and unit of work access:** both come only through `CasesSelector.newInstance()` and `Application.UnitOfWork.newInstance()`. This lets your `setMock` stubs replace them in tests.
- **Registered record:** the record passed to `registerDirty` is the loaded case itself, updated in place. A test that checks it with `fflib_Match.sObjectWith` on `IsEscalated` and `Priority` will therefore match.
- **Null-safe escalation check:** `IsEscalated == true` treats a mocked case with no value set as not escalated.
- **Status match:** the `Closed` check is an exact match on `Status`, as the spec says. `IsClosed` is not in the selector's field list, so other closed statuses are not detected.
- **Queue owners:** each task's `OwnerId` is copied from the case owner, as specified. If a case is owned by a queue, that task's insert will fail, because a Task cannot be owned by a queue.
- **Sharing:** the class is declared `with sharing`.

