The template uses static IDs, and LWC handles the scoping automatically:

- **ID scoping:** At render time, LWC rewrites template `id` values to be unique per component instance. It also rewrites IDREF attributes such as `aria-controls` in the same template to match. So `aria-controls` always resolves, even when several sections appear on one page.
- **`hidden` attribute:** It is bound to a boolean. When the value is `true`, LWC renders the attribute. When it is `false`, LWC removes the attribute entirely. The body `div` therefore stays in the DOM in both states.
- **`aria-expanded`:** It is bound to a getter that returns the string `"true"` or `"false"`, as the ARIA spec requires.

