/**
 * Turns an open NPSP pledge into a monthly installment plan.
 * Paid and written-off payments are kept as history. All other payments are replaced.
 */
public with sharing class PaymentPlanService {

    public class PaymentPlanException extends Exception {}

    public static List<npe01__OppPayment__c> scheduleInstallments(
        Id opportunityId,
        Integer numberOfPayments,
        Date firstPaymentDate
    ) {
        // Validate the inputs before touching any data.
        if (numberOfPayments == null || numberOfPayments < 1) {
            throw new PaymentPlanException('Number of payments must be at least 1.');
        }
        if (opportunityId == null) {
            throw new PaymentPlanException('An opportunity is required.');
        }
        if (firstPaymentDate == null) {
            throw new PaymentPlanException('A first payment date is required.');
        }

        // Lock the opportunity so two plans cannot be built for it at the same time.
        List<Opportunity> opps = [
            SELECT Id, Amount, IsClosed
            FROM Opportunity
            WHERE Id = :opportunityId
            WITH USER_MODE
            FOR UPDATE
        ];
        if (opps.isEmpty()) {
            throw new PaymentPlanException('Opportunity not found or not accessible.');
        }
        Opportunity opp = opps[0];
        if (opp.IsClosed) {
            throw new PaymentPlanException('Cannot schedule installments on a closed opportunity.');
        }

        // Paid and written-off payments reduce the outstanding amount.
        // Every other payment will be replaced.
        Decimal settled = 0;
        List<npe01__OppPayment__c> toDelete = new List<npe01__OppPayment__c>();
        for (npe01__OppPayment__c p : [
            SELECT Id, npe01__Payment_Amount__c, npe01__Paid__c, npe01__Written_Off__c
            FROM npe01__OppPayment__c
            WHERE npe01__Opportunity__c = :opportunityId
            WITH USER_MODE
        ]) {
            if (p.npe01__Paid__c == true || p.npe01__Written_Off__c == true) {
                settled += (p.npe01__Payment_Amount__c == null ? 0 : p.npe01__Payment_Amount__c);
            } else {
                toDelete.add(p);
            }
        }

        Decimal amount = opp.Amount == null ? 0 : opp.Amount;
        Decimal outstanding = amount - settled;
        if (outstanding <= 0) {
            throw new PaymentPlanException('There is no outstanding amount to schedule.');
        }

        // Split the amount: each payment is rounded down to the cent,
        // and the last payment absorbs the remainder.
        Decimal installment = outstanding.divide(numberOfPayments, 2, RoundingMode.DOWN);
        Decimal lastAmount = outstanding - installment * (numberOfPayments - 1);

        List<npe01__OppPayment__c> newPayments = new List<npe01__OppPayment__c>();
        for (Integer i = 0; i < numberOfPayments; i++) {
            newPayments.add(new npe01__OppPayment__c(
                npe01__Opportunity__c = opportunityId,
                npe01__Payment_Amount__c = (i == numberOfPayments - 1) ? lastAmount : installment,
                npe01__Scheduled_Date__c = firstPaymentDate.addMonths(i),
                npe01__Paid__c = false,
                npe01__Written_Off__c = false
            ));
        }

        // Delete before inserting so NPSP overpayment validation never sees both sets.
        // Roll back on any failure so nothing changes.
        Savepoint sp = Database.setSavepoint();
        try {
            if (!toDelete.isEmpty()) {
                Database.delete(toDelete, true, AccessLevel.USER_MODE);
            }
            Database.insert(newPayments, true, AccessLevel.USER_MODE);
        } catch (Exception e) {
            Database.rollback(sp);
            throw new PaymentPlanException('Could not schedule installments: ' + e.getMessage());
        }
        return newPayments;
    }
}
```

**Notes:**
- **Delete before insert:** the old open payments are deleted before the new ones are inserted. NPSP's payment validation therefore never sees the old and new payments together and treats them as an overpayment.
- **Rounding:** the last payment's amount is the outstanding amount minus the other payments. This makes the new payments add up exactly to the outstanding amount.
- **Locking:** the opportunity is read with `FOR UPDATE`, so two users cannot build plans on the same pledge at once.
- **Inputs:** the opportunity is queried without a subquery, because `FOR UPDATE` cannot be combined with one. A null opportunity Id or first payment date is rejected with a `PaymentPlanException`. A missing Amount counts as 0, which then fails the "nothing outstanding" check.
- **Security:** the class runs `with sharing`, and all queries and DML run in user mode, so the officer's own permissions apply.
- **No partial changes:** a savepoint undoes the delete if the insert fails. The error is re-thrown as a `PaymentPlanException`.

Two NPSP behaviours shape this design:

1. When an Opportunity is inserted with `npsp__Primary_Contact__c` set, NPSP's triggers usually create the Donor and Household Member contact roles. This depends on the org's household soft-credit settings.
2. When an Opportunity is inserted as Closed Won with NPSP Payments enabled, NPSP usually creates one payment automatically.

So the method does not blindly insert roles and a payment, because that could create duplicates. It inserts the Opportunity first, then reads what NPSP created and corrects it to the required end state. All of this runs inside a savepoint, so a failure leaves nothing half-created.

