Here is the class. It turns off only `TA_Contact_CreateWelcomeTask` through `MetadataTriggerHandler`'s action-level bypass, so `TA_Contact_FormatPhone` and all other Contact automation still run.

- **Bypass is always cleared:** the `try/finally` turns the bypass off even if the insert fails. Contacts inserted later in the same transaction then get their welcome task as usual.
- **Existing bypass is left alone:** if the bypass was already on before the call (set by an outer caller), the method leaves it on, so it doesn't undo someone else's setting.
- **Compile-time reference:** it passes the action's `System.Type` instead of a string name. A typo or a renamed class then fails at compile time instead of silently doing nothing.
- **Permission choice:** the insert runs in user mode, so the running user's field-level security and object permissions are enforced. If your migration user lacks some Contact field permissions, change this to `AccessLevel.SYSTEM_MODE`.

